module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DerivedQCoh.AffineDerivedEquivalence
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DerivedTildeEquivalence
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Duality.CompactGeneration

/-!
# The affine derived Spec–Γ equivalence, and the compact generator it transports

Let `R` be a commutative ring. `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/DerivedTildeEquivalence.lean`
constructs the derived sheafification–sections adjunction on `Spec R` between
`AlgebraicGeometry.derivedTilde R ⋙ ι`, with values in the *whole* of `D(𝒪_{Spec R})`, and
unbounded derived global sections `RΓ(Spec R, -)`. The two functors of [Stacks, Tag 06Z0] are
instead `derivedTilde R : D(R) ⥤ D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.derivedGlobalSectionsQuasicoherent R : D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R}) ⥤ D(R)`, and the
adjunction between *those* is `AlgebraicGeometry.derivedTildeQuasicoherentAdjunction`, the
restriction of the former along the fully faithful inclusion `ι` of the complexes with
quasi-coherent cohomology, which this file takes from
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DerivedQCoh.AffineDerivedEquivalence`.

With the adjunction in hand the tag's equivalence becomes an invertibility statement about its
unit and counit, and the file reduces it to exactly two inputs:

* the unit is invertible as soon as the degreewise comparison `Q(Γ(Spec R, M̃^•)) ⟶ RΓ(Q(M̃^•))`
  is, which is unbounded affine vanishing, [Stacks, Tag 08D4];
* the counit is invertible at an object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})` exactly when that object lies in
  the essential image of derived sheafification.

Each of the two implies half of the equivalence on its own — the unit gives full faithfulness and
the counit essential surjectivity — so the reductions are stated separately and then combined.

Finally the equivalence is put to the use it was wanted for: the compact generator of `D(R)` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Duality/CompactGeneration.lean` transports across it, giving the
affine case of [Stacks, Tag 09IS] — `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})` is compactly generated by the single
object `𝒪_{Spec R}[0] = derivedTilde R (R[0])` — and Brown representability over
`D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})`, [Stacks, Tag 0A8G].

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.derivedTildeQuasicoherentEquivalence` — the equivalence
  `D(R) ≌ D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})` whose functor is derived sheafification and whose inverse is
  derived global sections, available once derived sheafification is an equivalence.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.derivedTildeFullyFaithfulOfIsIsoUnit` — an invertible unit makes derived
  sheafification fully faithful.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.essSurj_derivedTilde_of_isIso_counit` — an invertible counit makes it
  essentially surjective.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.derivedTilde_isEquivalence_of_isIso_unit_of_isIso_counit` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.derivedTilde_isEquivalence_of_isIso_globalSectionsComplexComparison` — the
  two reductions of the tag's equivalence, the second stated at the hypothesis that unbounded
  affine vanishing supplies.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction_unit_app_of_isEquivalence` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction_counit_app_of_isEquivalence` —
  the converses, so that the three formulations are interchangeable.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_derivedTildeUnit` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_derivedTildeUnit` — **the affine case
  of [Stacks, Tag 09IS]**: `derivedTilde R (R[0])` is a compact object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})`
  and its shifts generate.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isTriangulated_rightAdjoint_derivedQuasicoherentSpec` — Brown
  representability over `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})`.

## Implementation notes

No `@[stacks]` attribute appears below. Tag 06Z0 is split into thirteen declarations, and a single
attribute anywhere in this cluster would mark the whole tag as formalized; what is proved here is
the
*adjunction* together with reductions of the equivalence, not the equivalence. The one input still
missing is recorded under "What is not done" below. No attribute for Tag 09IS either: that tag is
the statement for a quasi-compact, quasi-separated scheme, and only the affine case is reached
here, and only conditionally.

The adjunction is `CategoryTheory.Adjunction.restrictFullyFaithful` applied with `iC` the identity
of `D(R)` and `iD` the inclusion `ι`. Both commutation isomorphisms are `Iso.refl`: the left
adjoint of the derived sheafification–sections adjunction *is* `derivedTilde R ⋙ ι`, and
`derivedGlobalSectionsQuasicoherent R` *is* `ι ⋙ RΓ(Spec R, -)` by definition.

`CategoryTheory.Adjunction.map_restrictFullyFaithful_unit_app` and its counit companion would
identify the unit and counit of the restricted adjunction with those of the original one, since both
commutation isomorphisms are identities; that identification is *not* established below, and is
not needed. Every invertibility statement here is routed instead through full faithfulness and
essential surjectivity of `derivedTilde R`, which transports no morphism across the two
spellings.

The derived categories in force are the locally small ones, as everywhere in this cluster; see the
implementation notes of `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/DerivedTilde/Basic.lean` for why
`CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard` is not interchangeable with them, and why that is
forced rather than chosen for the compact-generation statements in particular.

## What is not done

The equivalence itself is not proved, and the hypothesis `(derivedTilde R).IsEquivalence` carried
by the results below is genuinely open in this repository. Three routes to it exist and all three
bottom out at the same place:

* through the unit, i.e. unbounded affine vanishing (Stacks 08D4): reduced in
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/AffineVanishingUnbounded/Tower.lean` to the affine case of
  Stacks 08D3, that an object of `D(𝒪_{Spec R})` is the derived limit of the tower of its
  truncations, which that file does not prove;
* through the counit, i.e. essential surjectivity of derived sheafification;
* through `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.derivedTilde_isEquivalence` in
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/DerivedQCoh/TildeFactorization.lean`, which asks that
  the Tag 06VT comparison functor over `Spec R` be an equivalence — the affine case of
  Stacks 08D9.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 06Z0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06Z0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08D4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08D4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08D9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08D9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A8G](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A8G)
-/

-- This file uses the locally small derived-category models below, which are not
-- global instances (see `StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedCategory.LocallySmall`):
-- `D(R)` for `R`-modules.
-- `D(𝒪_X)` for a scheme.
attribute [local instance] ModuleCat.hasDerivedCategory
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty Opposite

universe u u'

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

variable (R : CommRingCat.{u})

/-! ### The equivalence, reduced to the unit and the counit -/

/-- **An invertible unit makes derived sheafification fully faithful.** If the unit of the
derived sheafification–sections adjunction is invertible at every object of `D(R)` — which by
`AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction_unit_app` is unbounded affine
vanishing, [Stacks, Tag 08D4] — then `derivedTilde R` is fully faithful.

The unit makes `derivedTilde R ⋙ ι` fully faithful, and `ι` is faithful, so the first factor is
fully faithful as well. -/
def derivedTildeFullyFaithfulOfIsIsoUnit
    (hu : ∀ M : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R),
      IsIso ((derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction R).val.unit.app M)) :
    (derivedTilde R).FullyFaithful :=
  have : IsIso (derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction R).val.unit :=
    NatIso.isIso_of_isIso_app _
  Functor.FullyFaithful.ofCompFaithful
    (G := (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).ι)
    (derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction R).val.fullyFaithfulLOfIsIsoUnit

/-- **An invertible counit makes derived sheafification essentially surjective.** If the counit of
the derived sheafification–sections adjunction is invertible at `ι E` for every object `E`
of `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})`, then every such `E` is isomorphic to the derived sheafification of a
complex of `R`-modules.

Invertibility of the counit at `ι E` puts `ι E` in the essential image of `derivedTilde R ⋙ ι`,
and the resulting isomorphism descends along the fully faithful `ι`. -/
theorem essSurj_derivedTilde_of_isIso_counit
    (hc : ∀ E : (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
        (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).FullSubcategory,
      IsIso ((derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction R).val.counit.app
        ((DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
          (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).ι.obj E))) :
    (derivedTilde R).EssSurj where
  mem_essImage E := by
    have := hc E
    obtain ⟨M, ⟨e⟩⟩ := (derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction R).val.mem_essImage_of_counit_isIso
      ((DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
        (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).ι.obj E)
    exact ⟨M, ⟨(DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).fullyFaithfulι.preimageIso e⟩⟩

/-- **Tag 06Z0, reduced to its unit and counit.** Derived sheafification
`D(R) ⥤ D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})` is an equivalence as soon as the unit of the derived
sheafification–sections adjunction is invertible everywhere and its counit is invertible at every
complex with quasi-coherent cohomology. -/
theorem derivedTilde_isEquivalence_of_isIso_unit_of_isIso_counit
    (hu : ∀ M : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R),
      IsIso ((derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction R).val.unit.app M))
    (hc : ∀ E : (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
        (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).FullSubcategory,
      IsIso ((derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction R).val.counit.app
        ((DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
          (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).ι.obj E))) :
    (derivedTilde R).IsEquivalence :=
  ⟨(derivedTildeFullyFaithfulOfIsIsoUnit R hu).faithful,
    (derivedTildeFullyFaithfulOfIsIsoUnit R hu).full,
    essSurj_derivedTilde_of_isIso_counit R hc⟩

/-- **Tag 06Z0, reduced to unbounded affine vanishing and essential surjectivity.** Derived
sheafification is an equivalence as soon as the degreewise comparison
`Q(Γ(Spec R, M̃^•)) ⟶ RΓ(Spec R, Q(M̃^•))` is invertible for every cochain complex `M^•` of
`R`-modules — the affine case of [Stacks, Tag 08D4] — and the counit of the adjunction is
invertible at every complex with quasi-coherent cohomology.

The first hypothesis is the one
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/AffineVanishingUnbounded/Tower.lean` reduces to the affine case of
[Stacks, Tag 08D3]; the second is essential surjectivity. -/
theorem derivedTilde_isEquivalence_of_isIso_globalSectionsComplexComparison
    (h : ∀ M : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℤ,
      IsIso (globalSectionsComplexComparison (𝟙 (Spec R))
        (((tilde.functor R).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).obj M)))
    (hc : ∀ E : (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
        (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).FullSubcategory,
      IsIso ((derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction R).val.counit.app
        ((DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
          (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).ι.obj E))) :
    (derivedTilde R).IsEquivalence :=
  derivedTilde_isEquivalence_of_isIso_unit_of_isIso_counit R
    (isIso_derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction_unit_app R h) hc

/-! ### The three formulations are interchangeable -/

section

variable [(derivedTilde R).IsEquivalence]

omit [(derivedTilde R).IsEquivalence] in
/-- The unit of the derived sheafification–sections adjunction is invertible once derived
sheafification is an equivalence: the left adjoint `derivedTilde R ⋙ ι` is then fully faithful. -/
theorem isIso_derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction_unit_app_of_isEquivalence
    (M : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)) :
    IsIso ((derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction R).val.unit.app M) :=
  inferInstance

/-- The counit of the derived sheafification–sections adjunction is invertible at every
complex with quasi-coherent cohomology once derived sheafification is an equivalence: every such
complex is then in the essential image of the left adjoint. -/
theorem isIso_derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction_counit_app_of_isEquivalence
    (E : (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).FullSubcategory) :
    IsIso ((derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction R).val.counit.app
      ((DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
        (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).ι.obj E)) :=
  (derivedTildeGlobalSectionsAdjunction R).val.isIso_counit_app_of_iso
    (((DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).ι.mapIso
        ((derivedTilde R).objObjPreimageIso E)).symm)

/-- **The affine derived Spec–Γ equivalence, [Stacks, Tag 06Z0].** Derived sheafification and
derived global sections are mutually inverse equivalences between `D(R)` and
`D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})`, with the unit and counit of
`AlgebraicGeometry.derivedTildeQuasicoherentAdjunction` as the structure isomorphisms. Being
packaged from that adjunction, the functor is `derivedTilde R` and the inverse is
`derivedGlobalSectionsQuasicoherent R` on the nose. -/
def derivedTildeQuasicoherentEquivalence :
    DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R) ≌
      (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
        (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).FullSubcategory :=
  (derivedTildeQuasicoherentAdjunction R).toEquivalence

/-- The functor of `AlgebraicGeometry.derivedTildeQuasicoherentEquivalence` is derived
sheafification, hence additive. Supplied by name because instance search does not unfold the
equivalence. -/
instance derivedTildeQuasicoherentEquivalence_functor_additive :
    (derivedTildeQuasicoherentEquivalence R).functor.Additive :=
  inferInstanceAs (derivedTilde R).Additive

/-- The functor of `AlgebraicGeometry.derivedTildeQuasicoherentEquivalence` is derived
sheafification, hence commutes with the shift. Supplied by name for the same reason. -/
instance derivedTildeQuasicoherentEquivalence_functor_commShift :
    (derivedTildeQuasicoherentEquivalence R).functor.CommShift ℤ :=
  inferInstanceAs ((derivedTilde R).CommShift ℤ)

/-! ### The affine case of Tag 09IS -/

/-- **`derivedTilde R (R[q])` is a compact object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})`.** Granted the
equivalence of [Stacks, Tag 06Z0], the compactness of `R[q]` in `D(R)` — the easy half of
[Stacks, Tag 07LT], proved in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Duality/CompactGeneration.lean` — transports across it. -/
instance preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_derivedTildeUnit (q : ℤ) (J : Type u) :
    PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J)
      (preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op ((derivedTilde R).obj
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) q).obj (ModuleCat.of R R))))) :=
  have := Stacks.Duality.preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_derivedUnit R q J
  Stacks.Duality.preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_of_equivalence
    (derivedTildeQuasicoherentEquivalence R) _ J

/-- **The shifts of `derivedTilde R (R[0])` generate `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})`.** Granted the
equivalence of [Stacks, Tag 06Z0], the generation of `D(R)` by `R[0]` transports across it: an
object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})` receiving only zero morphisms from the shifts of
`derivedTilde R (R[0])` is zero.

Together with `AlgebraicGeometry.preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_derivedTildeUnit` this is the
affine case of [Stacks, Tag 09IS], the generator being `𝒪_{Spec R}` as the source says. -/
theorem isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_derivedTildeUnit
    (Y : (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).FullSubcategory)
    (hY : ((ofObj fun _ : PUnit.{u + 1} => (derivedTilde R).obj
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj
          (ModuleCat.of R R))).shiftClosure ℤ).rightOrthogonal Y) :
    IsZero Y :=
  Stacks.Duality.isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_map_of_equivalence
    (derivedTildeQuasicoherentEquivalence R)
    (Stacks.Duality.singleGenerator (ModuleCat.of R R))
    (Stacks.Duality.isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_derivedUnit R) Y hY

/-- `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})` has direct sums indexed by any type of the universe of its morphisms:
they are transported from `D(R)` along the equivalence of [Stacks, Tag 06Z0]. -/
theorem hasCoproducts_derivedQuasicoherentSpec :
    HasCoproducts.{u} (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).FullSubcategory := fun J =>
  have := Stacks.SmallDerivedCategory.hasCoproducts_derivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R) J
  Adjunction.hasColimitsOfShape_of_equivalence
    (derivedTildeQuasicoherentEquivalence R).inverse

/-- **Brown representability over `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})`, [Stacks, Tag 0A8G].** Granted the
equivalence of [Stacks, Tag 06Z0], every exact functor out of `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})` which commutes
with direct sums has a right adjoint, which is again exact: the category is compactly generated
by the single object `derivedTilde R (R[0])`.

This is the affine case of the statement [Stacks, Tag 09IS] is used for. -/
theorem exists_isTriangulated_rightAdjoint_derivedQuasicoherentSpec
    {D' : Type u'} [Category.{u} D'] [HasZeroObject D'] [Preadditive D'] [HasShift D' ℤ]
    [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D' n).Additive] [Pretriangulated D']
    (F : (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
        (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).FullSubcategory ⥤ D')
    [F.CommShift ℤ] [F.IsTriangulated]
    [∀ J : Type u, PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J) F] :
    ∃ (G : D' ⥤ (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
        (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).FullSubcategory)
      (adj : F ⊣ G) (_ : G.CommShift ℤ), adj.IsTriangulated := by
  have hcop := hasCoproducts_derivedQuasicoherentSpec R
  exact Pretriangulated.exists_isTriangulated_rightAdjoint_of_compactlyGenerated F
    (fun _ : PUnit.{u + 1} => (derivedTilde R).obj
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of R R)))
    (isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_derivedTildeUnit R)

end

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
